  m_Name: RamjetEngineData
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  engineName: Ramjet Engine
  engineDescription: A Ramjet Engine is an air-breathing reaction engine that produces
    thrust by compressing incoming air through the forward motion of the vehicle
    rather than using a mechanical compressor. It operates on the principle of ram
    compression, in which high-speed air is slowed and compressed as it passes through
    the inlet and diffuser. Its major components include the air inlet, diffuser,
    combustion chamber, fuel injection system, flame holder, and exhaust nozzle.
    During operation, high-speed air enters the inlet and is compressed as its velocity
    decreases. Fuel is then injected into the compressed air and burned in the combustion
    chamber. The resulting high-temperature gases expand through the exhaust nozzle
    and leave at high velocity, generating thrust. Ramjets are mainly used in high-speed
    missiles, experimental aircraft, and specialized aerospace propulsion systems.
    From an engineering perspective, inlet design, shock waves, pressure recovery,
    combustion stability, fuel-air mixing, thermal loading, nozzle expansion, and
    operating speed are critical factors affecting performance.
  engineCategory: Engineering
